config {
  type: "assertion",
  tags: ["meta", "monitoring"],
  description: "fct_meta_placement_daily must total what fct_meta_ad_daily holds, per day. The guard that the first placement feed needed and did not have — it ran for two months holding 0.7% of delivery while every assertion in the project passed."
}

-- An assertion FAILS if it returns rows. Empty result = healthy.
--
-- WHAT IT IS WATCHING FOR, in the words of what already happened.
-- platform_position_device_keboola, this feed's predecessor, requested
-- `actions` alongside the placement breakdowns. The extractor flattened
-- the actions array and the parent metrics row did not survive, so every
-- placement row carrying a click vanished and every row carrying none came
-- through with the correct value. The result was a report whose numbers
-- were right and whose volume was 0.7% of the truth.
--
-- Nothing caught it. Grain was unique, nothing was null, freshness was
-- current, the values that were present matched the API exactly. Only a
-- comparison against a total that is known to be complete finds this
-- class of failure, which is why that is what this does.
--
-- WHY ad-LEVEL IS THE RIGHT BASELINE. fct_meta_ad_daily comes from a
-- different vendor (Weld, ad_roas_insight) through a different pipeline,
-- and is reconciled in turn by assert_meta_spend_reconciliation. Two
-- independent paths to the same number.
--
-- TOLERANCE IS TWO-TIERED, and the second tier is not slack, it is a
-- measured fact about when each feed lands.
--
--   settled days, 3 or more back   0.5%
--   the last two closed days       5%
--
-- The two feeds are extracted hours apart -- Keboola wrote the placement
-- table at 02:18 on 2026-11-11, Dataform rebuilt the ad fact from Weld at
-- 03:30 -- and Meta restates recent days throughout. So the newest closed
-- day disagrees by ordinary timing, not by error. Measured 2026-11-11:
--
--   30 closed days, 29 EXACT on impressions, 30 exact on clicks
--   the single settled difference was 29 impressions of 13,183,790
--   the newest closed day, 10 November, sat at 0.9881
--
-- ONE TIER WOULD HAVE BEEN WRONG EITHER WAY. At 0.5% flat this fires
-- every morning on a difference that resolves itself by lunch, and an
-- assertion that cries daily is one nobody reads. At 5% flat it stops
-- watching the settled history, which is the part that stays wrong once
-- it goes wrong.
--
-- 5% IS STILL NOWHERE NEAR LOOSE. The failure this exists to catch put
-- 0.7% of delivery in the table -- a ratio of 0.007. A dropped account, a
-- lost dimension or `actions` back in the config all land in the same
-- territory. Nothing structural hides inside 5%.
--
-- THE CURRENT DAY IS EXCLUDED ENTIRELY. It is partial in both feeds by
-- definition and would fire every morning for no reason at all.

WITH plasament AS (
  SELECT
    date                      AS zi,
    SUM(impressions)          AS impresii,
    SUM(clicks)               AS clickuri
  FROM ${ref("fct_meta_placement_daily")}
  WHERE date < CURRENT_DATE()
  GROUP BY 1
),

nivel_ad AS (
  SELECT
    date                      AS zi,
    SUM(impressions)          AS impresii,
    SUM(clicks)               AS clickuri
  FROM ${ref("fct_meta_ad_daily")}
  WHERE date >= (SELECT MIN(date) FROM ${ref("fct_meta_placement_daily")} WHERE date < CURRENT_DATE())
    AND date < CURRENT_DATE()
  GROUP BY 1
)

SELECT
  a.zi,
  a.impresii                                  AS impresii_nivel_ad,
  IFNULL(p.impresii, 0)                       AS impresii_plasament,
  ROUND(SAFE_DIVIDE(IFNULL(p.impresii, 0), a.impresii), 4) AS raport,
  a.clickuri                                  AS clickuri_nivel_ad,
  IFNULL(p.clickuri, 0)                       AS clickuri_plasament,
  'fct_meta_placement_daily does not total fct_meta_ad_daily. A ratio well below 1 means the placement feed is dropping rows -- check first whether `actions` or `action_breakdowns` came back into the Keboola config, which is what broke its predecessor. A ratio above 1 means de-duplication in stg_meta_placement has stopped matching the source grain.' AS actiune
FROM nivel_ad a
LEFT JOIN plasament p USING (zi)
WHERE ABS(IFNULL(p.impresii, 0) - a.impresii) > a.impresii *
      IF(a.zi >= DATE_SUB(CURRENT_DATE(), INTERVAL 2 DAY), 0.05, 0.005)
